rong> Only mention tools and languages you\'ve truly used in projects, internships, or courses.</li>\n    <li><strong>Proof Over Buzzwords:</strong> Replace generic skill lists with specific project examples that demonstrate your abilities.</li>\n    <li><strong>Stand Out with Projects:</strong> Real-world experience makes your resume credible and memorable for recruiters.</li>\n    <li><strong>Common Mistakes Exposed:</strong> Learn what HRs instantly spot as red flags and how to fix them right now.</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <h2>Why Every Final-Year Student Needs to Watch This Now</h2>\n  <p>\n    As a final-year student, you’re likely battling project deadlines, placement anxiety, and the pressure to prove yourself. This video is a game changer for:\n  </p>\n  <ul>\n    <li><strong>B.Tech, MCA & BCA Students:</strong> Get clarity on creating resumes that reflect genuine coding and tech expertise—not just empty jargon.</li>\n    <li><strong>Freshers Facing Rejection:</strong> Understand why HRs dismiss \"skill-stuffed\" CVs and how you can instantly rise above the crowd.</li>\n    <li><strong>Aspiring Developers & Engineers:</strong> Learn to leverage your real projects as proof of skill, making you more attractive to employers.</li>\n    <li><strong>Students Stressed About Final-Year Projects:</strong> See how actual project demos (not just skill lists) give you an edge in interviews and campus placements.</li>\n    <li><strong>Those Seeking Honest Advice:</strong> Experience a no-nonsense breakdown of resume mistakes—delivered in a relatable, fun style that turns anxiety into confidence.</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <h2>Watch the Full Video on YouTube</h2>\n  <p>\n    Don’t let another opportunity slip by because of a \"Skill Buffet\" mistake. The full video explains exactly what recruiters look for—and what makes them hit \"reject\" in seconds.\n  </p>\n  <div style=\"position:relative;width:100%;padding-bottom:56.25%;height:0;overflow:hidden;margin-bottom:24px;\">\n    <iframe src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/RRbD9D4w-GY\" title=\"HRs REJECT Your Resume in 5 Seconds. Is This WHY? (The Skill Buffet Mistake)\" frameborder=\"0\" allowfullscreen style=\"position:absolute;top:0;left:0;width:100%;height:100%;\"></iframe>\n  </div>\n  <p style=\"text-align:center;\">\n    <a href=\"https://youtu.be/RRbD9D4w-GY\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Watch Now on YouTube</strong></a>\n  </p>\n\n  <h2>Continue Your Journey with FileMakr</h2>\n  <ul>\n    <li><a href=\"https://filemakr.com/source-code/php\" target=\"_blank\">Explore PHP Source Code Projects for Final Year</a></li>\n    <li><a href=\"https://filemakr.com/final-year-project-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">Get Inspiring Final Year Project Ideas</a></li>\n    <li><a href=\"https://filemakr.com/btech-final-year-project-report\" target=\"_blank\">Learn How to Write Impactful Project Reports</a></li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <h2>Your Top Questions Answered: Final Year FAQs</h2>\n\n  <h3>Why do HRs instantly reject resumes with long lists of skills?</h3>\n  <p>\n    Recruiters see generic skill lists as a red flag—often indicating copy-paste or lack of real experience. They want proof of where and how you used those skills.\n  </p>\n\n  <h3>What should I put in my resume if I have limited work experience?</h3>\n  <p>\n    Focus on academic projects, internships, or even personal coding assignments. Be specific about what technologies you used and what you accomplished.\n  </p>\n\n  <h3>How can I make my resume stand out during campus placements?</h3>\n  <p>\n    Highlight real projects with quantifiable outcomes instead of just listing programming languages or tools. Include links or short descriptions for added credibility.\n  </p>\n\n  <h3>Is it okay to mention skills I learned but haven\'t applied practically?</h3>\n  <p>\n    It’s best to include only those skills you\'ve actually used. Employers value practical application over theoretical knowledge.\n  </p>\n\n  <h3>I’m struggling with project ideas—what should I do?</h3>\n  <p>\n    Check out platforms like FileMakr for live demos and inspiration tailored for final-year students. Seeing real examples helps spark your own project direction.\n  </p>\n\n</body>\n</html>\n\n<!--\nSlug: /hrs-reject-your-resume-in-5-seconds-skill-buffet-mistake\n-->','Final-Year Students: Avoid Resume Rejection with Project-Driven CVs','HRs reject skill-stuffed resumes in 5 seconds! Learn to build project-driven CVs that stand out and land interviews. Watch now!','2025-07-02 14:34:32','resume-roaster','https://res.cloudinary.com/dikt4rnly/image/upload/v1751466813/mek3sagr7kf6ikt8rd8q.jpg','final year projects, resume tips for students, HR resume rejection, project-based resume, campus placement tips, fresher resume mistakes, skill buffet mistake, student CV tips, engineering resume guide, how to get hired as fresher','final year projects, resume tips, HR advice, project portfolio, campus placements, skill buffet, student jobs, fresher hiring, career guidance','Discover why HRs instantly reject skill-stuffed resumes. Learn how final-year students can build project-driven CVs that truly stand out!'),(32,'Smart Attendance – M.Tech Project Report with IEEE Standard Format','smart-attendance-mtech-project-report-with-ieee-standard-format','<!--\nSEO Meta Title: Smart Attendance M.Tech Project Report with IEEE Format – Full Source Code & Diagrams\nSEO Meta Description: Download the Smart Attendance final year M.Tech project report in IEEE format. Includes code, ER/DFD diagrams, Gantt chart, and high-scoring documentation—perfect for last-minute submissions. Get your report now!\n-->\n<p>Smart Attendance &ndash; M.Tech Project Report with IEEE Standard Format<!-- Slug URL --><!-- smart-attendance-mtech-project-report-ieee-format --></p>\n\n<h1>Smart Attendance &ndash; M.Tech Project Report with IEEE Standard Format</h1>\n\n<p><strong>&ldquo;I completed my final-year project in just 3 days using this code.&rdquo;</strong></p>\n\n<p>