art &amp; Gantt Chart.</li>\n	<li><strong>Real-World Tech Stack:</strong> Easily adapt to Java, Python Django, PHP Laravel or ASP.NET&mdash;sample code included.</li>\n	<li><strong>Testing Strategies:</strong> Structured unit, integration, black/white box test cases&mdash;easy to explain in viva.</li>\n	<li><strong>SDLC Model Coverage:</strong> Justify your planning with detailed SDLC lifecycle mapping.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>This package is more than just code&mdash;it&rsquo;s a fully guided journey from <strong>AIM</strong> to <strong>Conclusion</strong>, making it ideal for both coding newbies and advanced students alike.</p>\n\n<h2>Step-by-Step Overview of How It Works</h2>\n\n<p>The Payroll Management project is broken down into simple modules so you can explain every part during your presentation or viva:</p>\n\n<ul>\n	<li><strong>Introduction:</strong> Covers project aim, limitations of existing systems, why automation is needed &amp; feasibility studies.</li>\n	<li><strong>SRS (Software Requirements Specification):</strong> Outlines hardware/software needs for quick setup on college lab PCs.</li>\n	<li><strong>Design &amp; Planning:</strong>\n	<ul>\n		<li><em>ER Diagram:</em> Maps employee, salary slip, department relationships for database clarity.</li>\n		<li><em>DFD Diagram:</em> Visualizes payroll data flow from input to processing/output.</li>\n		<li><em>Waterfall Model:</em> Explains linear dev approach for easy marks in &quot;Why this model?&quot; questions.</li>\n	</ul>\n	</li>\n	<li><strong>Implementation:</strong> Shows front-end (HTML/CSS/Bootstrap) &amp; back-end (Java/PHP/Python) logic; database schema included.</li>\n	<li><strong>Testing:</strong> Vividly details all test cases so you can confidently answer any quality assurance query.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>The end result? A neat payroll system where admins can add employees, generate salary slips, and manage deductions without manual errors&mdash;a real-world scenario that impresses external reviewers!