CA Project Report with IEEE Format</p>\n\n<h1>Three Level Image Password Authentication &ndash; BCA Project Report with IEEE Standard Format</h1>\n<!-- Emotional Hook -->\n\n<p><strong>&ldquo;How I avoided rejection during project submission with this simple trick.&rdquo;</strong></p>\n\n<p>Ever felt that final-year panic? I did&mdash;until I stumbled on the <strong>Three Level Image Password Authentication</strong> project on FileMakr.com. With a polished IEEE-format report, all diagrams, and clean source code bundled together, my submission stress vanished overnight. <strong>If your project deadline is closing in, or you want a reliable way to ace your viva, this is your shortcut.</strong></p>\n\n<p><a class=\"cta-button\" href=\"https://filemakr.com/bca-final-year-project-report-three-level-image-password-authentication\">Jump to Download (Source Code + Report)</a></p>\n\n<h2>What Makes This Project Technically Impressive</h2>\n\n<p>The <strong>Three Level Image Password Authentication</strong> system isn&rsquo;t just another login page&mdash;it&rsquo;s a layered security mechanism combining classic password logic with visual authentication. Here&rsquo;s why professors love it:</p>\n\n<ul>\n	<li><strong>Multi-Factor Security:</strong> Uses images as authentication steps (not just text passwords), making brute-force attacks much harder.</li>\n	<li><strong>ER &amp; DFD Diagrams:</strong> Full database design and process flows included for better understanding and presentation.</li>\n	<li><strong>IEEE Standard Documentation:</strong> The report structure aligns perfectly with university guidelines&mdash;no formatting guesswork required.</li>\n	<li><strong>Waterfall Model Explored:</strong> Includes SDLC explanations, Gantt chart, feasibility study&mdash;everything your examiner expects.</li>\n	<li><strong>Coding in Multiple Languages:</strong> Source code is provided so you can adapt or demo easily (even if you&rsquo;re not a coding expert).</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>Step-by-Step Overview of How It Works</h2>\n\n<p>This system takes user authentication beyond basic passwords by implementing three distinct image-based verification levels:</p>\n\n<ul>\n	<li><strong>User Registration:</strong> User sets a traditional password plus selects three images from a secure gallery for each auth level.</li>\n	<li><strong>Login Attempt:</strong> User enters their ID/password, then is sequentially presented with three image sets&mdash;must pick the correct image at each step.</li>\n	<li><strong>Backend Verification:</strong> The backend cross-verifies the selected images using hashed values mapped in the database (ER diagram included in report).</li>\n	<li><strong>Access Grant/Reject:</strong> Only if all three image selections match the stored sequence is access granted&mdash;adding real-world security depth.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>The result? Even if someone knows your password, they can&rsquo;t log in unless they know your unique image sequence&mdash;a practical demo of layered security for your project viva!</p>\n\n<h2>See the App in Action</h2>\n\n<p>This preview lets you explore what&#39;s included in a complete academic report before downloading. It features ER Diagrams, DFD Diagrams, Flow Charts, and more&mdash;all professionally documented to showcase the project structure. Please note: this is a report-only preview and does not include the source code or live demo</p>\n\n<p><a class=\"cta-button\" href=\"https://www.filemakr.com/bca-final-year-project-report-three-level-image-password-authentication\" target=\"_blank\">View Demo &amp; Preview Screenshots</a><a href=\"https://online.visual-paradigm.com/share/book/sample-project-report-1uzumhkivv\">&nbsp;</a></p>\n\n<h2>Student Success Story &ndash; Real Testimonial</h2>\n\n<div class=\"testimonial-block\">&ldquo;I started working on my BCA project just two weeks before submission at NIT Jaipur. My coding skills weren&rsquo;t great and I was stressed about the documentation part. But after down