lete Documentation:</strong> Includes ER/DFD diagrams, Waterfall Model, Gantt Chart, SRS&mdash;everything you need.</li>\n	<li><strong>Real Database Design:</strong> Well-documented ER Diagram with entities like Customer, Appointment, Service, Staff.</li>\n	<li><strong>Flowcharts &amp; SDLC:</strong> Waterfall model planning and flowchart to demonstrate methodology knowledge.</li>\n	<li><strong>Testing Reports:</strong> Unit test cases, integration/system testing details for maximum marks.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>You&rsquo;ll also find a stepwise explanation of the <strong>existing vs. proposed system</strong>, feasibility study, hardware/software requirements, and a detailed work schedule&mdash;so you can answer any viva question confidently.</p>\n\n<h2>Step-by-Step Overview of How It Works</h2>\n\n<p>Here&rsquo;s how the Beauty Parlour Management project report guides you from scratch&mdash;even if you&rsquo;re under pressure:</p>\n\n<ol>\n	<li><strong>Introduction &amp; Problem Statement:</strong> Explains why managing appointments, staff scheduling, and services is vital for salons/parlours today.</li>\n	<li><strong>AIM &amp; Objectives:</strong> Clearly stated goals so your examiner sees focus and clarity from page one.</li>\n	<li><strong>SRS (Software Requirements Specification):</strong> Details hardware (RAM/CPU) and software stack needed&mdash;no guesswork on what to install or demo.</li>\n	<li><strong>ER/DFD Diagrams:</strong> Visualize user flows&mdash;like booking an appointment or assigning staff members&mdash;with polished diagrams ready to insert into your slides or viva handouts.</li>\n	<li><strong>SDLC &amp; Gantt Chart:</strong> Breaks down phases (Analysis &rarr; Design &rarr; Coding &rarr; Testing) and timelines so you can answer process-based questions instantly.</li>\n	<li><strong>Coding Section:</strong> Neatly organized source code (in C/C++/Java/PHP etc.)&mdash;ready to run and explain during demos or reviews.</li>\n	<li><strong>Testing &amp; Results:</strong> Includes real test cases (unit/integration/system), black box &amp; white box testing summary for those tricky examiner follow-ups.</li>\n	<li><strong>Bibliography/References:</strong> Proper citation so your report stands out as authentic and research-driven.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h2>See the App in Action &ndash; Live Demo &amp; Screenshots</h2>\n\n<p>This preview lets you explore what&#39;s included in a complete academic report before downloading. It features ER Diagrams, DFD Diagrams, Flow Charts, and more&mdash;all professionally documented to showcase the project structure. Please note: this is a report-only preview and does not include the source code or live demo<br />\n<a href=\"https://online.visual-paradigm.com/share/book/sample-project-report-1uzumhkivv\">Preview Demo (Read Only)&nbsp;</a></p>\n\n<p>Student Success Story &ndash; How I Scored Full Marks in My Viva at NIT Kurukshetra</p>\n\n<div class=\"testimonial\">\n<p><em>&quot;I was honestly panicking because I hadn&#39;t even started my project until two weeks before submission. Then I downloaded this Beauty Parlour Management report from FileMakr. Everything was there&mdash;ER diagrams, DFDs, proper SRS&hellip; even the SDLC phases were explained in such simple language! During my viva at NIT Kurukshetra (BCA batch), my panel kept asking about testing models&mdash;I just opened the report and answered directly from their test cases section.<br />\n<br />\nI ended up getting <strong>92% in my practicals</strong>. My professor even complimented me on how professional my documentation looked! I&rsquo;m now helping my friends crack their finals too.&quot;</em></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:right\">&ndash; Priya Sharma<br />\nBCA Final Year, NIT Kurukshetra</p>\n</div>\n\n<h2>Why It&rsquo;s Perfect for Your Final Year Submission</h2>\n\n<ul>\n	<li><strong>No Coding Experience Needed:</strong> The code is plug-and-play&mdash;run it directly or tweak it if you want bonus points.</li>\n	<li><strong>Y