tem-level programming. Here&rsquo;s what sets it apart:</p>\n\n<ul>\n	<li><strong>Real-Time Input Capture:</strong> Monitors all keyboard strokes and mouse actions efficiently&mdash;demonstrates event-driven programming and OS interaction.</li>\n	<li><strong>Comprehensive Diagrams:</strong> Includes ER Diagram, DFD Diagram, Flow Chart and Gantt Chart for clean documentation and easy viva explanation.</li>\n	<li><strong>Structured SDLC Approach:</strong> Built around the Waterfall Model and Software Requirement Specifications&mdash;helps you answer methodology questions confidently.</li>\n	<li><strong>Fully Documented Codebase:</strong> Source code is organized for quick understanding&mdash;even if you&rsquo;re new to system monitoring or input hooks.</li>\n	<li><strong>IEEE Standard Formatting:</strong> The report follows professional templates accepted by top universities and colleges.</li>\n	<li><strong>Testing Suite Included:</strong> Detailed unit, integration, black-box and white-box testing cases with results&mdash;essential for scoring in evaluation rounds.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>This project showcases practical skills in event handling, data logging, process flow design, and user activity analytics&mdash;all with a real-world use case professors love to see in B.Tech/MCA/BCA submissions.</p>\n\n<h2>Step-by-Step Overview of How It Works</h2>\n\n<ul>\n	<li><strong>User Launches Application:</strong> The app runs discreetly in the background after startup.</li>\n	<li><strong>Keyboard Event Logging:</strong> System hooks capture every keystroke in real-time using native APIs (demonstrates knowledge of low-level programming and event listeners).</li>\n	<li><strong>Mouse Movement Tracking:</strong> Mouse clicks and pointer movements are recorded&mdash;including timestamps for audit trails.</li>\n	<li><strong>Data Storage:</strong> All activity logs are securely saved to local files or a lightweight database (as per tech stack), demonstrating file I/O operations.</li>\n