sen front-end/back-end stack&mdash;easy to adapt for Java/Spring Boot or PHP/MySQL.</li>\n	<li><strong>Chapter V &ndash; Testing:</strong> Unit, Integration, Black/White Box test cases&mdash;all templates provided.</li>\n	<li><strong>Result &amp; Conclusion:</strong> Summarizes how the system meets its aim and advantages over manual gallery management.</li>\n	<li><strong>References/Bibliography:</strong> Cited as per IEEE guidelines for academic integrity.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>No need to write pages from scratch&mdash;just personalize your name and college logo!</p>\n\n<h2>See the App in Action</h2>\n\n<p>This preview lets you explore what&#39;s included in a complete academic report before downloading. It features ER Diagrams, DFD Diagrams, Flow Charts, and more&mdash;all professionally documented to showcase the project structure. Please note: this is a report-only preview and does not include the source code or live demo</p>\n\n<p><a class=\"cta-button\" href=\"https://www.filemakr.com/msc-final-year-project-report-art-gallery-management-system\" target=\"_blank\">View Live Demo Preview</a><a href=\"https://online.visual-paradigm.com/share/book/sample-project-report-1uzumhkivv\">&nbsp;</a></p>\n\n<p>The user dashboard is clean and follows modern GUI principles&mdash;perfect for demo day!</p>\n\n<h2>Student Success Story/Testimonial</h2>\n\n<div class=\"testimonial\">&ldquo;I was honestly panicking two weeks before my submission because my earlier idea got rejected! Then I found FileMakr&rsquo;s Art Gallery Management System package. I used their IEEE-formatted report and adapted the source code for my Java stack. Not only did I get a straight A in my viva at VIT Vellore (<em>M.Sc IT batch of &#39;24</em>) but my professor even asked if he could use my diagrams as examples for juniors! The DFDs were so clear that I breezed through every question in my internal review.&rdquo;<br />\n<br />\n<strong>&ndash; Neha Sharma<br />\nM.Sc IT, VIT Vellore</strong></div>\n\n<h2>